            <div xml:id="d527">

                <pb facs="0568" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg468"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760c.61/162b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d527-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-10"><hi rendition="#italic">August 10,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Following American note delivered to Italian Embassy this afternoon and given to
                    press for release morning papers August 11th. <pb facs="0569" n="469"
                        xml:id="pg469"/> Repeat textually to Paris, Rome, Berlin, Prague and Warsaw.
                    Send full summary to other European missions and to Helsingfors, Riga, Tiflis
                    and Constantinople. Latter for transmission to McCully, Sevastopol. Instruct in
                    all cases to give fullest possible publicity:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of note printed <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d527-f1" n="16" type="source" xml:id="d527-f1-content">
                <p>A similar telegram was sent on the same date to the Chargé in Japan with
                    instructions to “repeat textually to Peking and summarize to Vladivostok and
                    Harbin” (file no. 760c.61/162a).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
